WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.260
- Did you play football growing up?

00:00:01.260 --> 00:00:03.330
You look like a dude that
played football, just saying.

00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:04.430
- Well, thank you very much, Kelly.

00:00:04.430 --> 00:00:05.650
- I appreciate you saying that, but no.

00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:06.597
I did not.
- Oh!

00:00:07.546 --> 00:00:11.610
- I hit a really late growth
spurt later on in high school,

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:12.570
maybe even into college.

00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:14.620
And so when I was going into high school,

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:18.470
I played football one year in junior high,

00:00:18.470 --> 00:00:19.960
and I wanted to play
football in high school.

00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:22.480
And my dad... I was really, really skinny.

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:24.200
And my dad said, absolutely not.

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:25.610
You're not playing
football, they'll kill you.

00:00:25.610 --> 00:00:26.590
You'll be broken in half.

00:00:26.590 --> 00:00:27.989
Look at these guys,
they're twice your size.

00:00:27.989 --> 00:00:28.822
(Kelly laughing)

00:00:28.822 --> 00:00:31.130
And so, he was right and
it broke my heart for,

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:32.050
you know, five minutes.

00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:35.050
And then I just decided
I needed to do something.

00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:36.990
I wasn't going to sit
at home and do nothing.

00:00:36.990 --> 00:00:40.040
So, for the first time in my
life picked up a soccer ball.

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:40.930
I had a...

00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:42.783
It's interesting.

00:00:42.783 --> 00:00:45.890
We had a soccer field,

00:00:45.890 --> 00:00:48.520
literally right across
the street from our house.

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:49.353
And so I went over there

00:00:49.353 --> 00:00:51.270
and I taught myself how to play soccer

00:00:51.270 --> 00:00:53.080
in one summer, poorly.

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:58.080
I made the team, barely,
but that's my soccer story.

00:00:58.470 --> 00:01:00.500
- Oh, I love soccer. I
played soccer as well.

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:03.330
That's a fun sport. Now
it sounds like fat camp.

00:01:03.330 --> 00:01:05.210
Cause you just have to run a lot

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:06.296
because soccer -

00:01:06.296 --> 00:01:07.323
- Just running all over the place.

00:01:07.323 --> 00:01:09.030
- It's definitely a cardio sport.

00:01:09.030 --> 00:01:09.863
(Justin laughing)

00:01:09.863 --> 00:01:11.510
So, I loved it as a kid though.

00:01:11.510 --> 00:01:14.780
But have you ever coached
your daughter in any sports?

00:01:14.780 --> 00:01:16.500
- Yeah. You know? I did.

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:17.820
And I don't know why.

00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:19.550
Here we go about soccer again.

00:01:19.550 --> 00:01:21.910
I coached her when she was like, six,

00:01:21.910 --> 00:01:24.497
maybe six years old,
five or six years old,

00:01:24.497 --> 00:01:27.630
in a soccer league.

00:01:27.630 --> 00:01:30.460
And you know, when they're that age,

00:01:30.460 --> 00:01:32.850
what they're doing is, they're
just running after the ball.

00:01:32.850 --> 00:01:34.410
Wherever the ball goes,
that's where they're running.

00:01:34.410 --> 00:01:36.350
There's always like one kid,
maybe two kids on the team,

00:01:36.350 --> 00:01:37.370
that are really good and skilled

00:01:37.370 --> 00:01:39.230
and know what they're doing
even at that young age.

00:01:39.230 --> 00:01:40.368
My daughter was not one of them.

00:01:40.368 --> 00:01:41.810
(Kelly and audience laughing)

00:01:41.810 --> 00:01:44.600
But she had good team spirit and you know,

00:01:44.600 --> 00:01:45.960
they didn't keep score.

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:46.793
Nothing like that.

00:01:46.793 --> 00:01:47.626
They're five years old.

00:01:47.626 --> 00:01:49.210
These kids are just running
around trying to have fun.

00:01:49.210 --> 00:01:51.450
And there's always this one,

00:01:51.450 --> 00:01:54.259
at least one parent that just thinks,

00:01:54.259 --> 00:01:57.680
they think that their kid is, you know,

00:01:57.680 --> 00:02:00.650
a Messi or something, or Brett Favre,

00:02:00.650 --> 00:02:04.330
and they're going for the
touchdown in the Super Bowl.

00:02:04.330 --> 00:02:05.570
It's unbelievable.

00:02:05.570 --> 00:02:07.690
This guy would jump down my throat

00:02:07.690 --> 00:02:10.510
and he would run up and
down and ask questions,

00:02:10.510 --> 00:02:11.343
why this and why that?

00:02:11.343 --> 00:02:12.176
And I would just look at him.

00:02:12.176 --> 00:02:14.369
I go, "Dude, you know, we're
not even keeping score here?

00:02:14.369 --> 00:02:16.300
Put whatever score you want in your brain,

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:17.133
put it in your brain.

00:02:17.133 --> 00:02:17.966
That's what the score is."

00:02:17.966 --> 00:02:18.799
(Kelly laughing)
They're winning.

00:02:18.799 --> 00:02:19.632
Sure, they're winning, whatever.

00:02:19.632 --> 00:02:20.664
We're not keeping score.

00:02:20.664 --> 00:02:22.770
But he was into it.

00:02:22.770 --> 00:02:24.930
And I thought to myself, that
poor kid, when he goes home,

00:02:24.930 --> 00:02:26.460
I mean, his life was probably miserable.

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:27.700
It's probably the greatest
moment of his life

00:02:27.700 --> 00:02:29.010
to come play soccer

00:02:29.010 --> 00:02:33.090
and not have to worry about
his overbearing father.

00:02:33.090 --> 00:02:34.520
- Yeah. Oh my gosh.

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:36.080
It reminds me of that movie.

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:37.600
Was it "Kicking and Screaming"?

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:38.790
The Will Ferrell movie.

00:02:38.790 --> 00:02:42.065
Oh my God. I loved that movie.
- It's just like him.

00:02:42.065 --> 00:02:42.898
It sounds like him.

00:02:42.898 --> 00:02:44.120
- It's awesome. I grew up playing sports.

00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:45.270
There were definitely those parents.

00:02:45.270 --> 00:02:47.320
And I was like, no one's
going to the Olympics here,

00:02:47.320 --> 00:02:48.620
just so you're aware.

00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:50.640
- Exactly, let's just have some fun.

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:52.340
- They suck all the fun out of it.

